<%# Resize handle for the desktop sidebar (R1–R3, R8, R18, R20–R22).

  Rendered only when Avo.configuration.sidebar[:resizable] is on (the S5
  accessibility off-switch), and always with `hidden` present (R20). The
  sidebar_resize controller is the SINGLE owner of that attribute: it removes
  `hidden` on connect when the sidebar is open at >= lg, and re-adds it
  otherwise. So a cold load, a closed sidebar, or a no-JS visit each leave a
  correct, inert handle with no orphaned tab stop.

  aria-controls points at #main-sidebar — the layout wrapper carries that id and
  is the skip-link target; the .avo-sidebar it wraps has no id of its own.

  role="separator" forces role="presentation" onto any descendant, so the grip
  is a ::after pseudo-element in css/components/sidebar_resize.css, never a child
  node here.

  aria-valuenow / -valuemin / -valuemax are STATIC server values in this unit
  (Unit 8 makes valuenow track the drag). They are required, not optional:
  axe-core 4.12 lists aria-valuenow as a mandatory attribute of role="separator".
  With no stored width the value is the starting width — Avo's 256px unless the
  host set Avo.configuration.sidebar[:default_width]. %>
<% current_width = @sidebar_width || sidebar_width_default %>
<%= tag.div "",
  class: class_names("sidebar-resize-handle", "print:hidden": Avo.configuration.hide_layout_when_printing),
  hidden: true,
  role: "separator",
  tabindex: "0",
  title: t("avo.resize_sidebar_hint"),
  aria: {
    orientation: "vertical",
    controls: "main-sidebar",
    label: t("avo.resize_sidebar"),
    valuenow: current_width,
    valuemin: sidebar_width_min,
    valuemax: sidebar_width_max
  },
  data: {
    controller: "sidebar-resize",
    # Only the press is bound here. The controller attaches pointermove/up/cancel
    # to `window` for the duration of the drag rather than relying on
    # setPointerCapture to retarget them — see the note in startDrag.
    action: "pointerdown->sidebar-resize#startDrag dblclick->sidebar-resize#reset"
  } %>
